      {
        "ContentType": "Description",
        "SortOrder": 0,
        "Content": "12 Luí Na Greine, Naas Road, Kilcullen, Co. Kildare, R56 WK82\r\nImmaculate Four-Bedroom Semi-Detached Home with Private South-Facing Garden\r\nAppleton Property is delighted to present 12 Luí Na Greine to the market. This spacious four-bedroom semi-detached home extends to approximately 122 sq m and is situated in a highly regarded development on the Naas side of Kilcullen town.\r\nPresented in excellent turnkey condition, this attractive property offers bright, well-proportioned accommodation throughout and is ready for immediate occupation. The property is not in a chain, making it an appealing option for those seeking a straightforward purchase.\r\nThe accommodation comprises a welcoming entrance hallway with guest WC, a generous living room with a large bay window, open fireplace and double doors leading to the kitchen/dining room. The well-proportioned kitchen and dining area features extensive solid maple shaker-style fitted units, integrated appliances and a single-storey projection extending towards the rear garden. A separate utility room provides additional storage and convenient access to the side of the property.\r\nUpstairs, there are four bedrooms, including a spacious principal bedroom with a large bay window, two double built-in wardrobes and a modern ensuite shower room. The remaining bedrooms are well-proportioned, with Bedroom 4 currently arranged as a home office. A family bathroom, hot-press and attic storage complete the accommodation.\r\nThe property is approached via a cobble-locked driveway providing off-street parking for two cars, with mature evergreen hedging to both sides. A gated side entrance leads to the private, enclosed rear garden, which is primarily laid in lawn and enjoys a desirable south-facing aspect. The garden also features a block-built shed measuring approximately 2.4m x 2.0m, providing excellent storage and potential for use as a compact home office, subject to any necessary planning requirements.\r\nThe property benefits from gas-fired central heating, double-glazed windows, high-speed fibre broadband availability, a BER rating of C, a low-maintenance tiled façade and PVC rainwater goods.\r\nLuí Na Greine is a small and attractive development of semi-detached and detached homes on the periphery of Kilcullen town. Kilcullen offers a wide range of amenities for everyday living, including shops, cafés, restaurants, schools, sporting facilities and local services. Newbridge, with the Whitewater Shopping Centre, and Kildare Village are within easy reach, while a number of golf courses and leisure facilities are also located nearby.\r\nThe property is well positioned for access to the M9 and surrounding towns. Bus stops for Route 880, serving Naas and Carlow, and Routes 130/130A, serving Athy and Dublin, are located at the entrance to Luí Na Greine.\r\nThis beautifully maintained home is ideally suited to families, first-time buyers, commuters or those seeking a spacious, move-in-ready property in a well-connected location. We expect interest to be brisk. Interested parties are encouraged to act quickly to secure a viewing opportunity.\r\nViewing is strictly by appointment with the sole selling agent, Austin Egan of Appleton Property, Kilcullen."
      },
      {
        "ContentType": "Accommodation",
        "SortOrder": 1,
        "Content": "Entrance Hallway: 4.7m x 2.0m \r\n\r\nWide bright entrance hallway with glass panel to side of door. Solid oak flooring with turning staircase, guest wc, coving, alarm panel, gable window on landing providing additional natural light.\r\n\r\nLivingroom: 6.5m x 3.6m\r\n\r\nSpacious Livingroom with fresh carpeted floor, large bay window, window blinds, open fireplace with granite hearth, ornate light fitting, coving, double doors to kitchen/dining room. \r\n\r\nKitchen/Dining room: 6.5m x 5.8m\r\n\r\nPorcelain tiled kitchen floor with extensive solid maple shaker fitted kitchen units. Integrated dishwasher, integrated oven and four ring gas hob and extractor, integrated fridge freezer. \r\n\r\nSolid oak floor to dining area with patio doors to south facing rear garden. Curtains and poles, recessed lighting. \r\n\r\nUtility: 1.5m x 1.5m\r\n\r\nSeparate utility room plumbed for washing machine and dryer with additional storage and side door. \r\n\r\nGuest WC: 1.6m x 1.5m\r\n\r\nGround floor convenience with tiled floor, whb and vanity unit, wc, wall hung mirror, side window and recessed lighting. \r\n\r\nLanding: 4.0m x 3.0m\r\n\r\nSpacious landing with gable window providing natural light to landing and hallway below. Attic storage overhead. \r\n\r\nBedroom 1: 4.8m x 3.2m\r\n\r\nLarge double bedroom with fresh carpeted floor, very large bay window, two double built in wardrobes. Overlooking green area with mountain views, lamp sockets to bedsides, curtains poles and tie backs, ensuite bathroom.\r\n\r\nEnsuite: 1.8m x 1.6m\r\n\r\nModern ensuite, fully tiled floor to ceiling, shower off mains in enclosure, whb and pedestal, wc, wall hung mirror and extractor fan. \r\n\r\nBedroom 2: 3.7m x 3.0m\r\n\r\nSecond spacious double bedroom with carpeted floor, curtains and poles and window blinds. \r\n\r\nBedroom 3: 3.0m x 2.7m\r\n\r\nMid-size bedroom with carpet floor, window blind and built in wardrobe. \r\n\r\nBedroom 4: 3.0m x 2.6m\r\n\r\nTo rear, currently in use as a home office, with carpeted floor, window blind. \r\n\r\nBathroom: 1.8m x 1.8m\r\n\r\nTiled bathroom with wall-to-wall mirror, full bathroom suite with bath and Triton T90si shower, WHB and pedestal, WC.\r\n\r\nHotpress: \r\n\r\nShelved laundry storage area with factory insulated tank.\r\n\r\nGarden Shed: 2.4mx 2.0m\r\n\r\nBlock built garden shed suitable for conversion to single use home office if so desired. \r\n\r\nFront: Cobble locked front drive way with parking for two cars. With high mature planted evergreen borders to both sides. \r\n\r\nRear: Private rear garden, primarily in lawn with pebble path to area at rear with block built shed. Gated side entrance, South facing, with gated side entrance."
      },
      {
        "ContentType": "Features",
        "SortOrder": 3,
        "Content": "Spacious Four bedroomed home comprising c. 122 sq metres of internal living space\r\nBright light filled home with well-proportioned rooms throughout\r\nHigh Speed Fibre Broadband available. C BER Rating, Gas Fired Central Heating. \r\nExtensive fitted kitchen storage with integrated appliances and gas hob. \r\nWith utility room, three bathrooms, Block built garden shed suitable for home office. \r\nTurnkey home, immaculate, not in a chain, ready for immediate occupation on closing.\r\nOff street parking for two cars on cobble locked drive with mature hedging to both sides\r\nEnclosed private South facing rear garden with gated side entrance. \r\nHighly sought after development on the Naas side of Kilcullen, close to all amenities\r\nViewing Strictly by appointment with sole selling agent, Austin Egan of Appleton Property."
